  "title": "J, G and the silent H",
  "summary_es": {
    "en": "“j” is a throaty sound and “h” is silent.",
    "fr": "« j » est un son guttural et « h » est muet.",
    "zh": "“j”是喉音，“h”不发音。",
    "ja": "「j」はのどの音で、「h」は発音しません。"
  },
  "focus": "consonants",
  "sounds": [
    "x"
  ],
  "tip_es": "The letter “j”, and “g” before “e” or “i”, is a strong, throaty /x/, like the “ch” in Scottish “loch”. The letter “h” is always silent: hola sounds like “ola”. Do not pronounce “h” as in English “house”.",
